#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Within &quantaplus; there are several key concepts. To understand and take "
"advantage of &quantaplus;, you must first learn these concepts, the "
"fundamentals. This chapter will explain and show you these concepts, without "
"which &quantaplus; would be primitive."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Workspace"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&quantaplus; divides the workspace into three scopes: Global, Local, and "
"Project. These distinctions affect various components in &quantaplus;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: fundamentals.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid "Global"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Global items are available to anyone that uses &quantaplus;. From toolbars "
"to actions, everything marked as global is stored in the common &quantaplus; "
"folder structure. This has the effect of allowing a group of admins to save "
"certain toolbars, actions, and templates in the global tree, which can then "
"be used to keep a multi-user installation of &quantaplus; common to everyone "
"on the system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: fundamentals.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "Local"
msgstr "Local"

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Local items make up a single user's personal collection of web development "
"resources. These items are made up of a user's templates and toolbars. Local "
"items are stored in a user's home folder. This makes all of the user's Local "
"items available for personal use at instance."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: fundamentals.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "Project"
msgstr "Projècte"

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Project items are are only available to a particular project. These can be "
"anything from a &CSS; template to a toolbar with custom actions which "
"perform a special task on a project's files. Simply put, this is the most "
"limited scope. All of the items saved in the project workspace will be saved "
"in the project's folder tree, allowing you to share your specialized tools "
"and templates with whomever else you share your project with."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Multi-Document Interface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid "&quantaplus; editing the document you are now reading."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&quantaplus;' &MDI; is broken down into various parts: the editor window, "
"the quick info trees, informational tabs and the toolbars. Please see <xref "
"linkend=\"editor-3-2\"/>, <xref linkend=\"qit-3-2\"/>, <xref linkend="
"\"information-3-2\"/>, and <xref linkend=\"toolbars-3-2\"/> for more "
"information on these parts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Editor Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "&quantaplus;' editor window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&quantaplus;' editor window allows for multiple files to be opened at the "
"same time. When just one file is open, the document fills the entire editor "
"window. As soon as a second document is opened, a small amount of space is "
"taken from the bottom of the editor window to allow for tabs to be displayed "
"with the filenames and a status icon. The above picture shows a "
"<guiicon>floppy</guiicon> icon beside the filename, indicating that the file "
"has been modified and should be saved."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can right click on the tabs with the mouse to get a context menu with "
"entries related to the current document, like closing the current, other or "
"all tabs; switching to other tabs; reloading, deleting or uploading the "
"document; switching to a bookmarked line ; performing CVS operations on the "
"current document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Right clicking in the editor area will give you another context menu related "
"to the edited document content, like basic editing actions (cut/copy/paste), "
"editing the tag under the cursor, selecting the area covered by the tag "
"under the cursor, getting context help about the word under the cursor or "
"open a file if the string under the cursor points to a file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the top of the editor window is the editor toolbar set. Currently, "
"&quantaplus; defaults to &HTML; 4.01 Transitional, which has a default set "
"of toolbars that are loaded. As &quantaplus; progresses, the toolbars will "
"be updated to meet the needs of users and to make use of newer features."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Toolbar usage is pretty straight forward. If you want to insert a basic tag, "
"like &lt;p&gt;, into your document, then you can click on the icon that "
"represents the tag. Now you can insert your data for the tag you have just "
"inserted. If you wish to insert a tag that requires certain attributes (like "
"an anchor), then you will get a dialog box with the various fields for you "
"to fill in."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid "The anchor (&lt;a&gt;) dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Toolviews"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Toolviews."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Toolviews or Quick Info Trees (&QIT;) allow you to navigate, open, and "
"gather information in &quantaplus;. Its tabbed format presents you with the "
"Files, Project, Templates, Document Structure, Scripts, Attribute, and "
"Documentation Trees."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid "&QIT; Explained"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: fundamentals.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid "Files Tree"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is where you can browse your entire file system. You are presented with "
"two top-level roots of the file system. The first is your home folder and "
"the second is the filesystem root folder - /. Use these to find existing "
"files on your machine that you would like to edit or add to an active "
"project. Right mouse button clicking on a file in this view gives you "
"several options for managing the selected file and, also, allows you to "
"insert the file into an active project, if any, or toggle the view between "
"tree and list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: fundamentals.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "Project Tree"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"quanta-projects-3-2\">Project management</link> is one of "
"the many powerful tools that &quantaplus; offers. This tab displays all "
"files within your project and allows you to manage the files within the "
"project through the use of &RMB; clicking. Actions, such as add, remove, "
"upload, or delete files entirely from the disk, can be performed through "
"this menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: fundamentals.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid "Templates Tree"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Another feature of &quantaplus; is templates. Templates can be anything you "
"would like. Images, code snippets, an entire web page, et cetera. It is "
"entirely up to you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Templates are sorted into three categories, which are based on their scope "
"and the context they are being used. These scopes are carried over from "
"&quantaplus;' workspace. Global templates are usable all times, local "
"templates are usable to the current user, and project templates are usable "
"only within their specified project. More on templates can be found in <xref "
"linkend=\"templates-3-2\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: fundamentals.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scripts Tree"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you will find information about the various scripts available for use "
"by you. The Global, Local, and Project concept allows here as well. By &LMB; "
"clicking the entries, you gain access to all the available information about "
"the script. And &RMB; clicking allows you to perform a few actions, such as "
"running the script, editing the script, and mailing the script, for example."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: fundamentals.docbook:274
#, no-c-format
msgid "Document Structure Tree"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This tab displays the parser's internal representation of your document. By "
"&LMB; clicking on an element, your cursor will taken to the element's "
"position in the document. By &RMB; clicking on an element, you are presented "
"with a number of actions that deal with navigating and updating the tree."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: fundamentals.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>Attribute Tree</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This tree appears below all the other &QIT;s. Within it you can quickly edit "
"attributes and namespaces. The content-focused entry system allows you to "
"modify all the available attributes with little more than a few clicks of "
"the mouse."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Attribute Tree</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: fundamentals.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid "Documentation Tree"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:325
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can find complete documentation on web technologies to aid your "
"development. You can download pre-packaged documentation for &quantaplus; at "
"<ulink url=\"http://quanta.sourceforge.net/docs.html\">&quantaplus;' "
"documentation site</ulink>, you can <link linkend=\"creating-quanta-docs-3-2"
"\">create your own documentation</link>, and, by adding a folder named \"doc"
"\" to a project, you can add, edit, and view project-specific documentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:340
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Informational Tabs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid "&quantaplus;' Informational Tabs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default &quantaplus; has two tabs located at the bottom of the window "
"from which useful information can be obtained. These are the Messages window "
"and the Problems window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: fundamentals.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid "Messages Window Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This tab displays information from any scripts run in quanta. For example, "
"the DTD being used for the current document and any changes to the DTD are "
"displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: fundamentals.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "Problems Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This tab shows any errors in the markup of the current document. "
"&quantaplus; scripts which are executed will also print error messages (if "
"present) in this tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Toolbars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid "&quantaplus;' &HTML; toolbars."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:403
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&quantaplus;' toolbars have been extended greatly and are easy to "
"understand. You click on the button and you get an associated action from "
"that button. The beautiful part about toolbars is that you can define your "
"own actions graphically within &quantaplus;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:410
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Managing toolbars in &quantaplus; is easy. By selecting the <guimenu> "
"Toolbars</guimenu> menu, you have the options to load, save, add, remove, "
"and email toolbars. When you choose to load a toolbar, you may choose from "
"one of the three <link linkend=\"quanta-workspaces-3-2\">workspaces</link> "
"in &quantaplus;. When saving a newly created toolbar, you can save it in the "
"local scope or within a project's scope. If you would like to make a new "
"toolbar available in the global scope, ask your admin to place it in "
"&quantaplus;' global toolbar folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Another feature of &quantaplus; is the ability to email your toolbars. "
"&quantaplus; sends the toolbar as a gzipped tar archive through &kmail;. If "
"you receive a toolbar in email, then you can save (and load) it into "
"&quantaplus; like any other toolbar!"
msgstr ""
